{
  "assessment": "The diff introduces `config.mjs` and `merge.mjs` as new files but implements a shallow spread merge with reversed arguments, failing to layer user settings over defaults or deep-merge nested objects as specified.\n\n**Defect 1: Argument order in `loadConfig` causes defaults to overwrite user input.**\n- call: `node -e \"import('./config.mjs').then(m => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.loadConfig({ debug: true }))))\"`\n- expected: `{\"server\":{\"host\":\"localhost\",\"port\":8080},\"debug\":true}`\n- actual: `{\"server\":{\"host\":\"localhost\",\"port\":8080},\"debug\":false}`\n\n**Defect 2: `merge.mjs` uses a shallow operator that replaces nested objects entirely instead of merging them.**\n- call: `node -e \"import('./config.mjs').then(m => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.loadConfig({ server: { port: 9090 } }))))\"`\n- expected: `{\"server\":{\"host\":\"localhost\",\"port\":9090},\"debug\":false}`\n- actual: `{\"server\":{\"port\":9090},\"debug\":false}`\n\nThe change does not satisfy the task requirements for either deep merging or correct precedence ordering. Both defects are directly observable with the provided commands and contradict the stated behavior.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "{\"server\":{\"host\":\"localhost\",\"port\":8080},\"debug\":false}",
      "at": "config.mjs:9",
      "call": "node -e \"import('./config.mjs').then(m => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.loadConfig({ debug: true }))))\"",
      "defect": "Argument order in `loadConfig` causes defaults to overwrite user input.",
      "expected": "{\"server\":{\"host\":\"localhost\",\"port\":8080},\"debug\":true}"
    },
    {
      "actual": "{\"server\":{\"port\":9090},\"debug\":false}",
      "at": "merge.mjs:2",
      "call": "node -e \"import('./config.mjs').then(m => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.loadConfig({ server: { port: 9090 } }))))\"",
      "defect": "`merge.mjs` uses a shallow operator that replaces nested objects entirely instead of merging them.",
      "expected": "{\"server\":{\"host\":\"localhost\",\"port\":9090},\"debug\":false}"
    }
  ]
}
